# Raspberry Pi Pico W: the CYW43439 Wi-Fi chip on GPIO23 (WL_ON), 24 (DIO, also
# the chip's interrupt), 25 (CS) and 29 (CLK), driven by a PIO state machine.
# Its LED is on the Wi-Fi chip, not on a GPIO.
#
# The access points are what a scan finds and a join can succeed against:
#   apN=SSID,open[,RSSI[,CHAN]]  or  apN=SSID,wpa2,PASSPHRASE[,RSSI[,CHAN]]
board Pico-W

cyw43439 wifi on=23 dio=24 cs=25 clk=29 mac=28:cd:c1:00:00:01 ap1=TarteletteNet,wpa2,hunter22,-45,6 ap2=FreeCafe,open,-70,11

panel wifi at=0,0 span=3,2 label=Wi-Fi
